a family disturbance on the west side of  the valley ends in a deadly shooting it  happened last night on  spurt court that's near alta and buffalo  joe muller spoke to neighbors and has  this reaction  police say it appears the son in this  incident was acting in self-defense when  he allegedly shot and killed his father  now the shooting happened here  on spur court this all started around  six last night police say the father  involved attacked the son  and took off when police got here they  spoke with people in the house but could  not find the father  hours later around 10 30 metro got  another call after shots rang out they  say the father returned home  the son had shot the father the shooters  surrendered two officers and was  questioned  neighbors say they can't imagine an  argument leading to this hard to believe  my family is very close and we don't  argue so  hear people arguing like that and  getting to that point it's just  sad a few neighbors say they heard  several gunshots last night but  everyone was surprised when they heard  about what exactly happened  police did not say what the argument was  about the shooter is not in custody  police tell me since this is a  self-defense  case they do not expect charges to be  filed but the case was submitted to the  district attorney's office  for them to make the final decision  reporting near alton buffalo joe mohler  8 news now
 

